The MIT License grants rights to the underlying **source code and documentation only**. It does **not** grant rights to use the trademarked identity, brand assets, or logos of the Flicko project.

- **Brand Protection**: The names `"Flicko"`, `"Flicko App"`, `"Sonic Music"`, `"Aura AI"`, as well as associated logos, mascot art, iconography, sound marks, and visual design assets are exclusive proprietary marks of the project maintainers.
- **Forks & Derivative Works**: You are encouraged to build exciting products using this codebase. However, if you host a public instance, publish a mobile app, or distribute a derivative fork, you must remove all official Flicko branding, logos, and marketing imagery, and choose an independent name and identity.
- **No Implied Endorsement**: You may not use the Flicko name or marks in any manner that implies sponsorship, official partnership, or endorsement by the Flicko maintainers without prior written consent.

